# Osprey

The osprey is a large raptor found on every continent except Antarctica, and it
catches fish almost exclusively. It hunts on the wing, quartering high over open
water and hovering before a feet-first plunge that carries it briefly under
before it climbs straight out again; it cannot pursue a fish that it misses.
Spiny scales under the foot hold the catch, which is carried head-first to
reduce drag. See [[pandionidae]] and [[accipitriformes]].
